## Orpheon — https://github.com/kota-zo/Orpheon (GPL-3.0)

Valen reuses, with adaptation, the Spotify Web Player playback implementation and the hidden-page
plumbing of Orpheon (formerly Myspoti), by kota-zo and contributors:

- `libs/api` — the provider-neutral models and player/search contracts (`base/api`).
- `libs/web` — `PageHost`, `PageBridge`, `PageWatch` and cookie helpers (`base/api-web`).
- `libs/spotify` — `SpotifyApi`, `SpotifyPlayer`, the GraphQL catalog, `player-bridge.js` and the
  bridge plumbing (`base/api-spotify`).
- `libs/engine` — the native playback protocol types referenced by `api-spotify` (`base/engine`).
- `libs/ytmusic` — the YouTube Music page script, `YtmPage`, `InnerTube` and parsers (`base/api-ytmusic`).
- `host/desktop` — `CdpHost` / `CdpPageHost` (Chrome DevTools Protocol) (`base/host-cdp`).
- `host/android` — WebView hosts and the media-session/notification playback service (`base/host-android`).
  `SpotifyRelay` is a condensed port of Orpheon's `ControlRelay` (Spotify Connect requests sent from
  the app, without the WebView's `X-Requested-With`), whose finding it relies on. `BrowserIdentity` is a
  trimmed port of Orpheon's `Fingerprint` (user agent and client hints that agree).

Every source file carries its SPDX header. Orpheon's authors require credit, retention of notices, and
that derivative works are published under GPL-3.0 with complete source. Valen complies.

## Revera — https://github.com/caruno-git/Revera (GPL-3.0), pinned at c0b705c

Revera is a GPL-3.0 fork of Myspoti/Orpheon (`caruno-git/Revera`, `FORK.md`), and its visible fork
notice requires credit to Myspoti, retention of notices, and GPL-3.0 with published source for
derivatives. Valen complies: this code is GPL-3.0 and its source ships here.

- `host/android/.../LoginTransport.kt`, `PlatformStack.kt` and `LoginDiagnostics.kt` are ported,
  with adaptation, from Revera's `base/host-android/LoginTransport.kt`, `PlatformStack.kt` and
  `LoginErrorDetails.kt` at commit `c0b705c`. That is Revera's workaround (shipped in its 1.0.9) for
  Spotify's patched in-app sign-in: the sign-in page's `accounts.spotify.com` e-mail-code requests
  are sent from the app, without the WebView's `X-Requested-With`, and their `Set-Cookie` headers are
  written back into the page's cookie jar. `LoginDiagnostics` keeps only a stage, a host, an HTTP
  status or a failure type.
- `host/android/.../WebPlayerHost.kt`'s sign-in identity switch (the sign-in page as the phone's own
  mobile Chrome, the player page as the desktop Chrome, switched back as Spotify hands over) follows
  Revera's 1.0.2 sign-in fix (`configureLoginBrowser`/`configurePlayerBrowser`), still live at
  `c0b705c`; `MobileIdentity` in `BrowserIdentity.kt` is Valen's own expression of the same identity
  rule (its user agent and client hints must name the same browser).

The `X-Requested-With` finding itself dates from Orpheon/Valen (`SpotifyRelay`); Revera found the
sign-in form of it first. Revera's authors require credit to Myspoti and no relicensing; neither is
done here.

## Mochy Music — https://github.com/realidkroo/Mochy-Music (GPL-3.0)

Valen borrows design and implementation ideas, not files: the tight semi-bold type, the full-bleed
hero that fades into a black page, superellipse covers that share a curve with the surface holding
them (`ui/theme/Shapes.kt`, after Mochy's `SmoothCornerShape`), the floating capsule player and tab
bar, the cover's colours as soft drifting pools behind the player (`ui/components/Ambient.kt`,
after Mochy's ambient backdrop, including sampling the cover's left and right halves separately and
stepping the drift at 30 a second), and the sectioned drag-reorder queue. The code in those files is
Valen's own.

The playlist importer follows Mochy's matching approach (`core/…/TrackMatcher.kt`, after Mochy's
`importer/TrackMatcher.kt`): a normalised title and artist comparison, a duration term, a version
word that must agree, and an acceptance floor below which an entry is kept as unmatched rather than
replaced by the wrong song. Valen's scorer is its own code and stricter than Mochy's — a version
mismatch (remix, live, acoustic) scores zero outright, and a live-album pairing is capped below the
acceptance floor.

Liquid glass (`ui/components/Glass.kt`) takes Mochy's approach in `GlassKit` — record the content
once, let each glass surface draw the part under itself, blurred — onto Compose Multiplatform's
graphics layers, so it also draws on the desktop. The rim refraction shader, the droplet and the
light are Valen's own.

